## Examples

### File Download

```rust
use progress_rs::ProgressBar;

let bar = ProgressBar::new(file_size);
bar.set_message("download.zip");

while downloading {
    let chunk = download_chunk();
    bar.inc(chunk.len() as u64);
}

bar.finish_with_message("Complete!");
```

### Parallel Processing

```rust
use rayon::prelude::*;
use progress_rs::ParallelProgressIterator;

items.par_iter()
    .progress()
    .for_each(|item| {
        heavy_computation(item);
    });
```

### Hierarchical Progress

```rust
use progress_rs::MultiProgress;

let multi = MultiProgress::new();
let root = multi.add(1000, "Build Project");

let compile = root.add_child(500, "Compile");
let test = root.add_child(300, "Test");
let package = root.add_child(200, "Package");
```

## Performance

- **Zero overhead** when disabled (compile-time flag)
- **Lock-free** atomic operations for position updates
- **Debounced rendering** (default: 100ms)
- **Minimal allocations** - buffer reuse
- **Thread-safe** - Clone handles are cheap

